* Relay switching: pickup, bounce, hot pickup, release, and an armature held by remanence.
*
* Three relays of models/multiphysics/relay/relay_parts.va (200 Ohm, 2000-turn coil, a
* Jiles-Atherton core, a 1 mm air gap closed by a 2 g armature on a 200 N/m spring preloaded
* to 0.2 N), all driven by one coil voltage: 0 -> 30 V over 1 s, held 0.5 s, back to 0 over 1 s.
*   X1  coil at 20 C, armature travel 0.8 mm (a 0.2 mm residual gap when closed);
*   X2  the same at 85 C (coil resistance +25.5 %);
*   X3  coil at 20 C, travel 0.98 mm (a 20 um residual gap).
*
* Closed form, pickup: the armature leaves its backstop when the gap force Phi^2/(2 mu0 A)
* reaches the 0.2 N preload, at B = sqrt(2 mu0 F / A) = 0.15853 T, whatever the core; the
* current that takes depends on the core but not on the coil's temperature, so the hot coil
* needs R(85 C)/R(20 C) = 1.2555 times the voltage.
* What to look for (measured at 2.16.1+1; each coil reports lift-off, each armature its
* closing and opening):
*   lift-off at B = 0.15882 T (all three), i = 73.20 mA cold and 73.18 mA hot, at 14.657 V and
*     18.389 V: a ratio of 1.2547 (the 1.2555 of the resistances, less the coil's L di/dt).
*   the armature closes ~16 ms later and bounces once on the pole face.
*   release: X1 at 1.884 V, X2 at 2.455 V. X3 never releases: with only 20 um of air in the
*     closed circuit the core's remanence holds the armature shut at zero current -- why real
*     relays have a non-magnetic shim (the residual gap) on the pole face.
* Plot: python docs/examples/multiphysics/relay_plots.py target/release/va-cli
* Run: va-cli sim circuits/multiphysics/relay_switch.net --model models/multiphysics/relay --tran --report x1,x2,x3,c
VA20 a20 gnd DC 293.15
VA85 a85 gnd DC 358.15
VC c gnd PWL(0 0 1 30 1.5 30 2.5 0 3 0)
X1 c gnd x1 th1 relay_coil
XA1 x1 c armature xmax=0.8e-3
XT1 th1 a20 coil_thermal
X2 c gnd x2 th2 relay_coil
XA2 x2 c armature xmax=0.8e-3
XT2 th2 a85 coil_thermal
X3 c gnd x3 th3 relay_coil
XA3 x3 c armature xmax=0.98e-3
XT3 th3 a20 coil_thermal
.tran 100u 3
.end
